meta {
  name: Send Message
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/contact
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Recruiter",
    "email": "hiring@example.com",
    "message": "We have a role that matches your background, can we talk?"
  }
}

docs {
  # Send Message

  Public. Rate limited to **5 requests per 15 minutes per IP**, because every
  accepted message costs an email.

  | Field | Rule |
  | --- | --- |
  | `name` | 2–80 characters |
  | `email` | must parse as an email; trimmed and lowercased before use |
  | `message` | 20–2000 characters |
  | `website` | honeypot, must be absent or blank |

  ## Honeypot

  The form renders `website` hidden, so a real visitor always leaves it blank.
  Send it filled and the API answers **200 with the same message** but mails
  nothing — a bot cannot tell the difference, so it has nothing to retry.

  | Status | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 | accepted (or silently dropped as spam) |
  | 422 | `VALIDATION_ERROR` — includes a `details` array |
  | 429 | `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` |
  | 502 | `MAIL_SEND_FAILED` — Resend rejected it |
  | 503 | `MAIL_NOT_CONFIGURED` — no `RESEND_API_KEY` / `CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL` |
}
